FFmpeg's Windows Media Audio decoder (versions 1 and 2), cut from FFmpeg n7.1.1
(commit db69d06eeeab4f46da15030a80d539efb4503ca8)
https://ffmpeg.org/
Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 or later; see COPYING.LGPLv2.1.

Vendored unmodified from the tag above, in libavcodec/:
  wmadec.c wma.c wma.h wma_common.c wma_common.h wma_freqs.c wma_freqs.h wmadata.h

Cut from the tag above:
  libavcodec/aactab_scalefactor.c  the scale factor code tables from libavcodec/aactab.c (the only part of
                                   that file the decoder uses), with its license header

Written for rct3pp, LGPL-2.1-or-later, standing in for the parts of FFmpeg the decoder expects around it:
  libavutil/*.h, libavcodec/avcodec.h codec_internal.h config_components.h decode.h get_bits.h internal.h
  put_bits.h sinewin.h
                     small versions of FFmpeg's headers: the structures and helpers the decoder uses, a
                     bounds-checked bit reader and a tree-walking VLC reader
  compat.c           float vector helpers, sine windows, the inverse MDCT and the VLC table builders
  rct3_wma.h rct3_wma.c
                     the C interface rct3pp calls: open a decoder for a stream's format, decode a packet

It is compiled as C17 into the rct3pp binary; nothing of FFmpeg is linked from the system.
